---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import EmailCapture from "../components/EmailCapture.astro";

const title = "Sanctum · The AI council for your firm and your family.";
---

<Base
    title={title}
    description="A multi-agent AI council that runs entirely on hardware you own. Built to operate a venture capital firm with absolute confidentiality, and robust enough to run your home."
>
    <main>
        <p class="tagline">Coming soon · founder beta</p>

        <h1>Your firm already has a brain.<br />It just doesn't know it yet.</h1>

        <p class="lede">
            Sanctum is a council of local AI agents that runs on hardware
            you own, operating with zero cloud dependencies. No OpenAI API bills. No "your data may be used to improve our models." 
            Total sovereignty over your startup's secrets, your LP communications, and your family's data.
        </p>

        <EmailCapture listName="founders" />

        <hr />

        <p class="muted">
            Built for the founder, the VC, and the parent who demands absolute privacy and is wondering when AI will finally operate on their terms.
        </p>

        <h2>The Triptyq Capital Story</h2>
        <p>
            At Triptyq Capital, we don't just invest in the future; we run our venture firm on it. 
            Sanctum was forged in the fires of high-stakes deal flows and LP negotiations. 
            Our agents brief us on pitch decks before board meetings, parse complex financial models, and orchestrate our entire fund's intelligence—all while remaining completely isolated from the public cloud. 
            If it's confidential enough for our LPs, it requires Sanctum.
        </p>

        <img src="/jcrm-ui.jpg" alt="JCRM UI featuring Squido Studio portfolio profile" class="screenshot" />

        <h2>One Council. Two Worlds.</h2>
        <p>
            A multi-agent architecture featuring specialized entities orchestrated through a single voice interface on your phone.
        </p>
        
        <h3>For the Startup & Firm</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Absolute Confidentiality:</strong> Analyze proprietary codebases, pitch decks, and cap tables without leaking IP to third-party models.</li>
            <li><strong>The Briefing:</strong> Your council pre-reads your deal flow and briefs you on your commute.</li>
            <li><strong>Institutional Memory:</strong> An encrypted, locally vectorized RAG pipeline that remembers every meeting, term sheet, and founder interaction.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>For the Haus</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Infrastructure & Security:</strong> Enforces screen-time policies locally (even when Apple's Screen Time is flaky) and guards the network.</li>
            <li><strong>Family Logistics:</strong> Coordinates schedules, answers your Apple Watch from the park, and acts as the ultimate home operating system.</li>
            <li><strong>Offline Resilience:</strong> When the WiFi goes down or the cloud has an outage, your council still works.</li>
        </ul>

        <hr />

        <h2>What you get</h2>

        <h3>Sanctum Core — free, open source</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>The council: eight distinct agents, voice-accessible via your phone</li>
            <li>The cathedral: local Qwen 3.6 35B inference at 50+ tokens/sec on an M-series Mac</li>
            <li>Force Flow: your network's nervous system; routes alerts, watches the watchers</li>
            <li>mTLS everywhere: every internal connection mutually authenticated</li>
            <li>No telemetry. We don't know if you're running it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="muted">
            License: FSL-1.1-MIT (auto-converts to MIT after 2 years).
        </p>

        <h3>Sanctum Founder Pass — $129, lifetime</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Holocron mobile + iPad app, seamlessly syncing with your council via Tailscale</li>
            <li>Cross-device encrypted memory sync (your own R2 / B2 bucket)</li>
            <li>Pre-trained agent personalities and voice profiles tailored for executives</li>
            <li>Multi-haus federation (office, chalet, in-laws, dorm rooms)</li>
            <li>Founder support, direct email, six months</li>
            <li><strong>Triptyq Capital Portfolio & LPs:</strong> Lifetime free access for all our portfolio founders (and yes, our LPs too 😉).</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="muted">One payment. No subscription. Yours forever.</p>

        <h2>Who's behind this</h2>
        <p>
            We are Guillaume Therien, Bertrand Nepveu, Charles Sylvestre, and Joe Tou — the four General Partners at Triptyq Capital. 
            But more importantly, we are four dads raising kids in a rapidly accelerating technological world.
        </p>
        <p>
            We built Sanctum as the ultimate solution for our own work-life balance. It's the AI council that manages our venture firm by day, and protects our hausholds by night. 
            It briefs us on our deal flow before board meetings. It answers our Apple Watches from the park. It even locks the network when our teenagers try to bypass their screen-time limits.
        </p>
        <p>
            We are building Sanctum because we demand that it exists. The business
            model is "we can't keep maintaining this for free, but we refuse
            to make it depend on the cloud." A one-time payment for
            premium features pays for the engineering time. The open-source core stays
            free forever.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <h2>Get notified when v1 ships</h2>
        <EmailCapture listName="general" />
    </main>
</Base>
